.TH START-MU2EDAQ-NOTIFY-SERVER.SH 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-phone-notification-system 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
start-mu2edaq-notify-server.sh \- start the notification server in the background
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./start-mu2edaq-notify-server.sh
.RI [ server-option ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Changes to the repository root, runs
.BR bootstrap.sh (1)
if
.I venv/bin/mu2edaq-notify-server
is missing, and exits 0 without doing anything if the pid in
.I data/notify-server.pid
is alive. Otherwise it starts
.B mu2edaq\-notify\-server \-\-config
.I CONFIG
under
.BR nohup (1),
appending output to
.IR data/notify-server.log ,
records the pid, waits one second, and reports whether the process is still
alive.
.PP
This is not a supervisor: nothing restarts the server if it exits later.
On the current production host the server is run instead by a per\-user
launchd agent,
.BR org.mu2edaq.notify-server ,
whose plist is not kept in this repository; see
.IR docs/OPERATIONS.md .
.SH OPTIONS
Every argument is passed to
.BR mu2edaq-notify-server (1)
after
.BR \-\-config ,
so it overrides the configuration file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I data/notify-server.pid
Pid of the background server.
.TP
.I data/notify-server.log
Server stdout and stderr, appended.
.TP
.I config/notify-server.yaml
Default configuration.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_CONFIG
Configuration file (default
.IR config/notify-server.yaml ).
.PP
All other
.B MU2EDAQ_NOTIFY_*
variables reach the server; see
.BR mu2edaq-notify-server (1).
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 when the server is running after one second, or was already running.
1 when it exited within that second; the last 20 log lines are printed to
stderr and the pid file is removed. A server that dies later is not detected.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
\&./start\-mu2edaq\-notify\-server.sh
\&./start\-mu2edaq\-notify\-server.sh \-\-no\-tls \-\-port 9000
tail \-f data/notify\-server.log
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR stop-mu2edaq-notify-server.sh (1),
.BR mu2edaq-notify-server (1),
.BR start-mu2edaq-notify-chain.sh (1)
.SH AUTHOR
